      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T02:02:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Simply since adding `static_assert(sizeof(unsigned long) \u003d\u003d 4, \"Unsignled long not 4 bytes\");` gives me a compile error, `unsigned long` and `uint32_t` are not the same. So, theoretically `using unsigned long` might be good in that there is no need to truncate it.\n\nIn practice, when I run the Genshin trace, `truncating to 32bits` and `using unsigned long` do not show a diff in term of function duration. \nSo,, difficult to say which one is better.",
      "parentUuid": "cfd277ac_40341067",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "1959cc73ac8371bc890e614a68df17bb2c44a782",
